<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fourteen Points</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fourteen Points were a statement of principles for peace issued by US President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodrow-wilson">Woodrow Wilson</a> in 1918. They called for self-determination, including autonomous development for the peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a>, encouraging national movements that contributed to the break-up of the Austro-Hungarian Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fourteen-points.jpg" alt="Fourteen Points" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Orpen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_Orpen_Woodrow_Wilson_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
